Yes, it does seem that API has been a little slow on getting faster
CPUs out to the public.  Soon IBM will be making copper interconnect
alphas and they'll have their MHz edge back.  Until then, you've done
the smart thing and actually tested your own applications...

I have too, but the performance difference is more like 600+%, so the
alphas are a real value for me.

You may want to investigate whether a UP2000 with its 6-way crossbar
switch (2 procs, 2 256 bit wide banks of memory and 2 pci buses) is
of any benefit to your codes.  More bandwidth is sometimes better
than more MHz.

If I were trying to make a big purchasing decision like this, I
think I'd buy about half of the cluster now and the other half later.

BTW, RAM prices are set to go up by ~25% soon.

Good luck,

Tony Hammitt


