To be sure, it targets something that isn't a strength of the Alpha
toolset.  

If your plans involve a processing load primarily oriented to compiling
the Linux kernel, it would indeed be dumb to buy Alpha systems for the
purpose.

Part of that may lie in GCC not being quite as well-tuned on Alpha
as it is on IA-32.  

