Two ways to fix this:

Knock the fifo size down to 3 MB:

cdrecord -v fs=3m cdimage.iso

or increase the shared memory maximum:

echo 5000000 > /proc/sys/kernel/shmmax

which only works on >= 2.2 version kernels and is not persistent
through rebooting.

Using the 3MB fifo size is easier...  The problem is that the
standard limit to the shared memory size segment on alphas is
set to 4072K, not the 4096k that cdrecord tries to use.

Has anyone looked at 2.4?  Is this always going to be a problem?

Regards,

Tony Hammitt



