>was going to try first.  Maybe Linux would be a little more friendly to
>someone who doesn't know what they're doing.

  Linux boots fine from both SRM and ARC. ARC needs something called milo, 
which will boot the linux kernel for you. It's not kludgy, it's very 
configurable, and it works fine. SRM requires that you use BSD disklabels. 
I've used both on my SX164, but only ARC on my pc164 because my video card
had issues with the SRM console. If you are going to use SRM you need to make
sure that you update to the latest firmware image.
  Check out www.alphalinux.org, there's alot of good info there. 

  Eric


