Assuming that you are using SRM, check what options you are using to
boot the system ( type 'show boot*') at the console.. If the variable
boot_file is set to /boot/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0 change it to the new kernel
and you should be fine. 

If you are using aboot ( no boot_file value and boot_osflags set to
'0'), boot up linux and edit /etc/aboot.conf to point to the new
kernel..

If you are using Alphabios/ARC/MILO ... I don't know

