MPICH's performance is icky.  Try getting MPI/Pro's free MPI implementation
instead, it works much better (2X better scaling for our applicaiton)

>
>Another problem is that our kernel that supports 4GB of RAM for the 264DP is
>rather unstable (2.2.14smp). Very often, the machines freeze when running
>mpi programs. Is anybody aware of a stable SMP kernel that supports acces to
>4GB of RAM on 264DP systems ?

There are about 30 billion different things that could be wrong with your
system, from hardware to software.  Try to isolate a very simple test case
that is totally reproducible.  For example, programs which do lots of I/O
over the network, or fill up lots of memory.  You should try to figure
out if the kernel is Oopsing, or is the hardware actually hanging, etc.
I just spent a week debugging a device driver that completely hung the
system due to a very simple bug (overwriting the 8K kernel stack by
allocating too much local memory in a function).  The system went into
a hard lock without any messages from the kernel.

Dave



