Xavier,

    I had this same problem with performance, but found that it may be in other
areas other than mpi.  I take it you are using redhat linux (my hint was the
2.2.14smp kernel :).  You may be interested to find that the compiler that you
are using (if you are using gcc) is not optimized for the alpha architecture
(or your are not using the options that tell the gcc compiler to optimize the
code).  One of solutions that I found to this problem was to use the compaq
compilers that are made freely available for enthuasist usage in addition to
compiler options.  The can be found on compaq's website.  If I am way off, or
you have already tried this route, then I appologize for wasting your time (and
mine).
    With respect to your question on the 2.2.14smp kernel you are using,
I would suggest downloading 2.2.16 and building it with the specific options
that you need.  A good howto can be found at
http://charlotte.redhat.com/support/docs/rhl/kernel-upgrade/kernel-upgrade-5.html

and replacing the make config with make menuconfig or make xconfig if you have
x running.

Mathew Lee
