>init_mm.
>
>The question now is how to tell the respective kernel part to activate this
>sym..

I reported this to the kernel maintainer mailing list, and Alan
Cox says this is fixed in 2.2.15.  For kernel 2.2.13, the
solution is to apply the context diff below to kernel/ksyms.c,
then recompile the kernel (make boot), boot from that kernel,
then rebuild and install the modules (make modules ; make modules
install).

*** usr-src-linux-kernel-ksyms.c	2000/05/26 23:17:34	1.2
--- usr-src-linux-kernel-ksyms.c	2000/05/26 23:18:35	1.3
***************
*** 416,418 ****
--- 416,421 ----
  
  /* init task, for moving kthread roots - ought to export a function ?? */
  EXPORT_SYMBOL(init_task_union);
+ 
+ /* Added by Rob Riches, 5/26/00.  Module bttv needs init_mm */
+ EXPORT_SYMBOL(init_mm);

Good luck,

Robert Riches
