I was wrong, the machine boot with a tape in but only if 
aboot is launched "slowly" :

From the SRM console :
- If aboot is started non-interactively, the kernel is 
launched immediatly ; the system hangs because the tape drive 
had not enough time to be initialized.

- If aboot is started interactively, you must wait
  2 or 3 seconds and you can boot. And that works !

So the solution is to put a SRM "boot_osflags"
without any references with the file /etc/aboot.conf, in order
to start aboot interactively. Let the tape drive be initialized
and boot. :-)

Aboot has no option to start a timeout before launching
the kernel, isn't it ?

I think a timeout will be a solution. 


