Hi Mike.

Mike wrote:
> I have to make a boot disk from my distribution (SuSE).

Nope. The image  you installed on the hd acts as 'bootdisk'. What you
need is an initial ramdisk image (e.g. 'root1440.img' for a debian
installation).

> After booting the image on my hd it asks me for an image disk, this is the
> one from SuSE.

There should also be a diskette from SuSE containing a compressed initrd
image.

> Does the booting image on hd have to match the distribution?

Not exactly, but the kernel versions should match.

hth & Greets
  Michael Keller
