I had the same problem a few weeks ago...

This one was answered on the axp-list@redhat.com end of last year.
(This list is searchable at www.alphalinux.org)

Force the ess driver to type 1688 or 1868.
When loading the sb.o module you can specify esstype=XXXX.
Alternatively I compiled the driver into the kernel and simply edited
sb.c to force the esstype.

Have fun,
	Peter


