Michael Champigny (champign@cadosf.hlo.dec.com) wrote:
: Also, another gotcha when
: you get further...when formatting the disk with fdisk/minlabel, leave
: the last block untouched (use total-1) otherwise you'll wrap around
: and blow away an aboot sector.

It is fixed in fdisk from current versions of util-linux (say from 2.10f
and up, I think, maybe earlier).  The deal is simple - if fdisk suggests
that it will allocate for you cylinders with numbers highers than what
you have on a disk, and it tells you correctly how much you have, then
do not agree.  Not very surprisingly this does not work too well.

  Michal



